---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import SignatureFormatterTool from '../../components/tools/SignatureFormatterTool';
---

<ToolLayout
	title="Signature Formatter - Crop and resize for forms | TommyTools"
	description="Format a signature image: crop, set dimensions, pick PNG/JPEG/WebP, optional max KB, and preview it. Runs in your browser. No acceptance claims."
	heading="Signature formatter"
	purpose="Crop and resize a signature for online forms, convert format, optionally target a max file size, and preview on a plain background. This does not guarantee acceptance by any institution."
	category="Photo & signature"
	categoryHref="/#cat-photo-signature"
>
	<div slot="tool">
		<SignatureFormatterTool client:load />
	</div>

	<div slot="instructions">
		<ol>
			<li>Choose a signature image from your device.</li>
			<li>
				Optional: pick a <strong>verified preset</strong> if one is listed (sourced + dated). Otherwise
				enter the form’s width, height, format, and max KB yourself.
			</li>
			<li>Drag the crop box or its corner handles (touch-friendly) to frame the ink.</li>
			<li>Choose format and preview background, then <strong>Update preview</strong> or download.</li>
		</ol>
	</div>

	<div slot="example">
		<p>
			Example: crop tightly around ink, export <strong>300×80 PNG</strong> on white. If a form asks for
			under 40 KB, set max KB - the tool reports honestly if the limit cannot be met.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div slot="formula">
		<p>
			Crop pixels → draw onto a plain-background canvas at the requested size → encode as PNG, JPEG, or
			WebP. Optional luminance threshold maps light/dark for contrast. Max KB uses the same iterative
			quality/scale approach as the compressor (PNG: scale steps only).
		</p>
	</div>

	<div slot="limitations">
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Not an official stamp.</strong> Matching dimensions or file size does not mean a form
				will accept the signature.
			</li>
			<li>
				Verified presets only appear when checked against a trustworthy source with a verification date.
				None are shipped until then - use manual specs from the form.
			</li>
			<li>Threshold is a simple contrast aid, not automatic background erasure.</li>
			<li>Very large images may be slow on phones; keep files under the stated size limit when possible.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>


	<div slot="related">
		<ul class="related-list">
			<li><a href="/tools/image-resizer">Image resizer</a></li>
			<li><a href="/tools/image-compressor">Image compressor</a></li>
		</ul>
	</div>

</ToolLayout>
